## Security and Authorization

- Passwords are hashed using bcrypt before being stored.
- User sessions are stored in PostgreSQL.
- Protected routes require an authenticated session.
- Recipe ownership is determined by the logged-in user's database ID.
- Users cannot edit or delete recipes belonging to other accounts.
- SQL queries use parameterized values to help prevent SQL injection.
- Password hashes